  "description": "The Rose Backroad GRX 820 is an adventure gravel bike with carbon frame that puts the focus on comfort, versatility and cargo capacity. Thanks to features such as the generous tyre clearance of 53 mm, a frame compartment, a detachable frame bag and a USB-C port under the handlebar, it is the perfect companion for long tours in versatile terrain or bikepacking. Characteristics and advantages: The Backroad GRX 820 weighs just about 9.6 kg1 and features the mechanical Shimano GRX RX820 1x12 groupset with a 40-tooth chainring up front and a 10–51-tooth cassette at the rear. The shifting system remains independent from power or batteries, is easy to maintain and features a particularly light mountain gear that allows even untrained riders to tackle long, steep climbs. + Carbon gravel bike at an entry-level price + Mechanical shifting without a battery + Light mountain gear for steep climbs Ideal for: • anyone looking for a versatile carbon gravel bike at an attractive entry-level price • sporty gravel tours and multi-day bikepacking • long climbs and changing terrain • tours on tarmac and rough gravel • riders looking for comfort and control on long distances Less suitable for: • gravel racing with a focus on maximum aerodynamics • technical MTB trails or aggressive off-road riding • short rides focused purely on city riding or everyday use Highlights: • Magnetic Fidlock bag system – including a precisely fitting frame bag (approx. 3 litres) • Integrated frame compartment – space for tools and equipment, including a tool bag • USB-C charging port – power supply directly on the handlebar (power bank required) • 18 attachment points – flexible mounting of bottles, bags and other accessories • Tyre clearance up to 53 mm – more damping and grip on rough terrain • Carbon seat post with a low clamp – comfort through flex Other features: The Backroad GRX 825 Di2 features Continental’s 45 mm-wide Terra Adventure tyres fitted on robust Rose G30 aluminium wheels (25 mm inner rim width). A chainguide protects against chain drops and the fi´zi:k Terra Argo X7 saddle ensures sportiness and comfort. The Rose handlebar and stem also allow for attachment of additional parts such as an aerobar or a computer mount. Note: Pedals are not included. ¹ may vary up to +/- 5 % due to manufacturing tolerances, reference frame colour lions mane, size M/L, without pedals and bags",
